# Everything `zig build` produces: the install prefix (the demo binaries, and
# the docs from `zig build docs`) and the local build cache. Both are derived
# from the source in this repo, and the cache is worse than stale elsewhere -
# it holds absolute paths from this checkout and objects for this toolchain,
# so it is wrong on another machine before it is even out of date.
zig-out/
.zig-cache/
# What that cache was called before Zig 0.13, in case an older toolchain runs.
zig-cache/

# Where `zig fetch` puts a dependency's source for this checkout. Derived
# from the url and hash in build.zig.zon, and re-fetched from those, so it
# is the package cache rather than anything this repo owns.
zig-pkg/

# Ad-hoc builds that bypass `zig build` - `zig build-exe`, `zig build-lib`,
# `zig test some_file.zig` - drop their output next to the source instead.
*.exe
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.exp
*.obj
*.o
*.lib
*.a
*.dll
*.so
*.so.*
*.dylib
*.wasm

# What a run that ended badly leaves behind. Large, machine-specific, and
# worth nothing once the bug it came from is fixed.
core
core.*
*.stackdump
vgcore.*

# Editor and tooling leavings. `.cache/` is clangd's index, which grows to
# tens of megabytes and is rebuilt from the source anyway.
.vscode/
.idea/
.vs/
.zed/
.cache/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS leavings.
.DS_Store
._*
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
